{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/test/clax/http_api_real_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:27:36.541404Z","id":"61e06d8099e33a774b00da0bfe8bbe18eb11445bfeadcf00a7f9fb72869365a8","body":{"detail":"The daemon is stopped in a try/finally inside the test body (lines 178-181). When the test hits its 3-minute timeout, package:test abandons the body and the finally never runs, so the clax child (started with Process.start, not killed when flutter test exits) keeps running. _Daemon.start (lines 225-265) kills the process only on its own 90 s deadline: an HttpException or any exception other than FormatException/SocketException from the /healthz probe escapes the loop with the process still alive. Register the stop with addTearDown right after Process.start (and kill by p.pid in start's catch-all), which runs on timeout too. The scratch home is also under Directory.systemTemp (line 198) rather than under the worktree's target/ as the repository's test rules ask.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":16},"end":{"line":21},"content_hash":"b6c3a3d4f7aa94ac3b3437f6e671bd7d4eb228834098843f5d63df1c5b3231e5"},"summary":"The real-daemon test can leave its daemon running","tags":["review","test-hygiene","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/test/clax/http_api_real_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:33:52.334399Z","id":"63849714ba47c1a2d5abe1ceb65dc544995d51cb683fa6694e35a25358217b0b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:191a54d9","summary":"Fixed: http_api_real_test.dart registers the daemon's stop (SIGTERM, SIGKILL after 10 s) with addTearDown right after Process.start, kills the child on any exception in start, treats any IOException from the health probe as not-yet-up, and keeps its scratch home under target/flutter-app/ (removed in a tear-down). CLAX_TEST_BIN=... flutter test test/clax: +64 all passed; no clax-api-real-* left under target/flutter-app.","supersedes":"61e06d8099e33a774b00da0bfe8bbe18eb11445bfeadcf00a7f9fb72869365a8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/test/clax/sse_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:35:59.590088Z","id":"0745c589f27864448a1db49d83a7ce69a0b33be2568daa7a97124c61780e44a8","body":{"detail":"Both tests set eventConnectTimeout or eventIdleTimeout to 50 ms of wall time and then assert exactly one retry (delays == [500 ms]). A healthy second connection that takes longer than 50 ms to answer, or a body chunk that arrives more than 50 ms after its headers, adds a retry and fails the assertion. They passed 14 of 14 runs here, 6 of them alongside ten busy loops, so this is a risk, not a failure seen. AGENTS.md asks for injected clocks for timing rules; reconnectingSse could take a timer factory (or the tests run under fake_async) so the deadlines fire on command.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":296},"end":{"line":378},"content_hash":"df654bf128e01c0f9784bd21259c80be99278dd82585ef6343c6dc8cec912122"},"summary":"The connect and idle deadline tests run on 50 ms real timers","tags":["review","test-hygiene","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
